To test the lowest 10% missing case, we simulate a 10% lowest-value-missing scenario on the validation data set, and select the shift correction parameter value that produces the smallest validation error. In reality, we may not know the actual ranges and amounts of low values missing in the testing data, and thus cannot simulate the situation on the validation data precisely. For a range of the lowest-value-missing scenarios where half of the lowest 5%, 10%, 20%, and 30% values are missing, we impute with a single \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
